# Runtime dependency contract — Phase 8.7-D.1-CORRECTION-3 (Finding E).
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH for what the service containers install.  The compiled,
# fully-transitive, hash-pinned lock is `requirements-runtime.txt`
# (generated — do not edit by hand):
#
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#       -o requirements-runtime.txt requirements-runtime.in
#
# Both service Dockerfiles install ONLY `requirements-runtime.txt` with
# `pip install --require-hashes` — no broad `>=` ranges, no unpinned
# transitive resolution at build time, no divergence between the test and
# container environments for the shared packages (enforced structurally by
# the dependency-parity guard; mutation M29).
#
# WHY THESE EXACT PINS (the deliberately chosen compatible set — the
# "last verified generation" the security test suite runs warning-free):
#
# * fastapi 0.128.8 / starlette 0.52.1 — the last pre-starlette-1.0
#   generation.  starlette 1.x deprecates the httpx-based TestClient the
#   whole security suite is built on ("install httpx2"); the gateway and
#   agent apps run identically on either generation, so the CONTAINER is
#   deliberately held on the verified generation too — one compatible set,
#   not two drifting worlds.
# * anyio 4.12.1 — anyio 4.15+ deprecates the `anyio.abc.BlockingPortal`
#   alias that starlette 0.52's TestClient imports (verified: 4.13/4.14
#   clean, 4.15 emits a deprecation warning).
# * pydantic 2.14.1 / redis 8.1.0 / requests 2.34.2 / PyJWT 2.15.1 — the
#   versions the resolved test lock carries; pinned so the runtime and
#   test locks share identical versions for every shared package.
#
# The remaining runtime dependencies keep their documented minimums; the
# lock resolves their full transitive closure with hashes.
#
# UPDATE PROCEDURE (documented, not ad-hoc): change a pin here, re-run the
# pip-compile command above on Python 3.11, regenerate requirements-test.txt
# the same way, and let the dependency-parity guard + the fresh-venv CI
# verification prove the two locks still share the pinned runtime set.

